AC4 — isolating the PAP-1659 effect
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  abstains       : 126 -> 126   (UNCHANGED, 34.8% of photos)
  confident-wrong:  26 ->  26   (UNCHANGED,  7.2% of photos)
  budgetExhausted fires: 0 / 362

  Mechanism, not just the count. Every PAP-1659 hunk in gearCounter.js is behind
  a `Date.now() >= deadline` test (lines 1079, 1241, 1372, 1432, 1484, 2783,
  2834, 3085) with `deadline = t2 + WALL_CLOCK_BUDGET_MS`, WALL_CLOCK_BUDGET_MS
  = 45000 (line 95), anchored after decode+preprocess (PAP-1683 fix B). The
  slowest photo in the corpus is 5074ms — 8.9x of headroom to the deadline; not
  one photo comes within 5x of it. Every guarded branch is therefore statically
  unreachable on this corpus at host speed, and the observed identity is the
  expected consequence, not a coincidence.

  This was pre-registered on the issue BEFORE the numbers landed, from reading
  the 49a7498..HEAD diff: predicted 210/362 = 58.0%, abstain 126, conf-wrong 26,
  unchanged to the photo. That is exactly what came back.

  The other accuracy-adjacent changes in the range are also inert here, for the
  same kind of reason:
   - preprocess() extracted to a backend seam (PAP-1694, aec054c/8f77b27) — the
     JS backend is the default and its calls are byte-identical to the previously
     inlined four (rgbaToGray -> clahe(3.0,8,8) -> gaussianBlur5x5 ->
     cannyEdges(50,150)).
   - rBins hoisted out of the grid loop + .fill(0) — maxRadius is loop-invariant.
   - PAP-1662 (7666e47) is Sentry-only.

